    rdf:value """to the Medici tombs and the Pazzi Chapel, then called on Mrs. Chapman, who had just bought a bronze Venus made by the Venetian forger, Marini, who took me in six years ago. Also dressmaker’s.
A nice evening to ourselves.
Friday May 8. 1903. I Tatti Settignano
Lunched at Mrs. Ross’ to meet a rich American, Mr. Rogers, whom Bernhard positively  abhorred . While we were there a telegram came from Jephson saying he was coming to us tomorrow. We both think he is in trouble, engagement fallen through, or something. But I  hope not. I hope it is only friendliness. Still, I can never have any confidence again that he is really frank with me, and his not telling me of his engagement until after 5 months has put a complete barrier between any intimate even friendship, although """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 194 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1902-03> .

